    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65096" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάρτῠρος</span></b> , ὁ, 
			Ep.
		 form for <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάρτυς, ἐστὲ μάρτυροι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.302
				</span></i>
			, etc.; also in Central Greece, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(1).226
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Drymaea</span>), <i><span class="en">
				364
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Naupactus</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				1684
			</span></i>, al. (Delph.), etc.: sg. once in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷσιν ἄρα Ζεὺς μάρτυρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					16.423
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PGen.</u>
				54.6
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A.D.)</span>. (<i><span class="en">
				Zenod.
			</span></i> rejected this form, but it is defended in Sch. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				1087.22
			</span></i>.)</div>
